      "subject": "Re: Quick question | byLLM structured output",
      "message": "Hi Priya,\n\nThanks for inquiring about byLLM for your log triage pipeline.\n\nTo answer your question: byLLM returns the model response as text. To get the structured fields (severity, component, message), you can prompt the model to output JSON. If your provider supports it (like OpenAI), enabling \"JSON mode\" is highly recommended to ensure valid structure.\n\nWhile byLLM doesn't natively parse this into typed objects out-of-the-box, the JSON format allows for easy deserialization in your pipeline, avoiding the need for manual text parsing.\n\nLet me know if you need assistance with the prompt configuration.\n\nBest regards,\nJaseci Team"
    }
